        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खेल (khel) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from khel, \"play\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL lists Old Marwari khelaï under it (CDIAL 3918). It is the noun of the verb khelṇo, \"to play\". CDIAL says that if Sanskrit krīḍati, \"plays\", is of non-Aryan origin, these forms may share its source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
